  {
    "page_content": "5. Order Intake Recognition and Measurement\n5.1 Recognition Criteria for Order Intake\nAn order shall be recognized as Order Intake when ALL of the following conditions are met:\n- A legally binding contract or Purchase Order (PO) exists, AND\n- The order value can be reliably measured, AND\n- Collectability is reasonably assured (see 5.3).\nKEY CHANGE FROM v1.0\nCollectability is now a recognition precondition, not merely a downstream approval trigger.\nCFO POLICY FRAMEWORK | CONTROLLED DOCUMENT Page 2",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "C:\\Users\\USER\\Desktop\\RAG\\output_pdfs\\POL-ORD-001_v2.0_Order-Intake-Recognition-Measurement.pdf",
      "page_number": 2,
      "extraction_method": "text",
      "doc_id": "POL-ORD-001_v2.0",
      "doc_type": "policy",
      "policy_id": "POL-ORD-001",
      "version": "2.0",
      "status": "ACTIVE",
      "is_current": true,
      "control_id": "CTRL-REV-014",
      "process_area": "Order-to-Cash (O2C)",
      "owner": "Group Finance – Revenue Assurance",
      "effective_date": "2025-01",
      "superseded_date": null,
      "supersedes": "POL-ORD-001_v1.0",
      "superseded_by": null,
      "audit_cycle": null,
      "date_prepared": null,
      "tests_policy_id": null,
