  {
    "page_content": "5.2 Customer Commitment\nCustomer commitment must be evidenced by BOTH:\n- A signed Purchase Order\n- A countersigned contract\nOrders supported by a PO alone do NOT qualify for recognition.\n5.3 Collectability Assessment\n5.3.1 Risk Scoring Model\nCollectability is assessed using a combined weighted risk score:\nRisk Score = (0.40 × Credit Rating Score) + (0.35 × Payment History Score) + (0.25 × Country Risk Score)\nEach component is scored on a 0–100 scale. Credit Rating Score is derived from Group Credit Risk classification;\nPayment History Score is based on trailing 12-month payment behavior; Country Risk Score is published quarterly by\nGroup Treasury.",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "C:\\Users\\USER\\Desktop\\RAG\\output_pdfs\\POL-ORD-001_v2.0_Order-Intake-Recognition-Measurement.pdf",
      "page_number": 3,
      "extraction_method": "text",
      "doc_id": "POL-ORD-001_v2.0",
      "doc_type": "policy",
      "policy_id": "POL-ORD-001",
      "version": "2.0",
      "status": "ACTIVE",
      "is_current": true,
      "control_id": "CTRL-REV-014",
      "process_area": "Order-to-Cash (O2C)",
      "owner": "Group Finance – Revenue Assurance",
      "effective_date": "2025-01",
      "superseded_date": null,
      "supersedes": "POL-ORD-001_v1.0",
      "superseded_by": null,
      "audit_cycle": null,
      "date_prepared": null,
