  {
    "page_content": "5.3.2 Escalation Requirements\nOrders scoring below 50 require MANDATORY Regional Finance Head sign-off prior to booking.\n5.4 Timing for Booking of Order Intake\nOrder Intake shall be booked ONLY once BOTH of the following are received and verified by Finance:\n- Signed Purchase Order\n- Countersigned contract\n5.5 Orders in Non-Euro Currencies\n5.5.1 Conversion Methodology\nConverted Order Value (EUR) = Order Value (Local Currency) ÷ Month-End Spot Rate\nThe Month-End Spot Rate is published by Group Treasury as of the booking date.\n5.5.2 FX Variance Control\n-\nFX Variance (%) = |Booking Rate Order Date Rate| ÷ Order Date Rate × 100\nIf FX Variance (%) > 5%, the order must be:\n- Flagged in the system\n- Routed to the Controller for review prior to final booking\n6. Order Intake Approvals",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "C:\\Users\\USER\\Desktop\\RAG\\output_pdfs\\POL-ORD-001_v2.0_Order-Intake-Recognition-Measurement.pdf",
